{
  "title": "Parenthetical quantities create junk ingredient measurements",
  "description": "During a pipeline snapshot audit on 2026-04-22, several \
snapshots preserved the source `raw` ingredient text correctly but generated \
extra `measurements` entries from parenthetical quantities that are either \
yield hints or alternate units. Those parsed measurements are incomplete or \
wrong enough to be misleading.\n\
\n\
Concrete examples:\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/smittenkitchen-com_2009-09-grilled-lamb-kebabs-tzatziki.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/smittenkitchen-com_2009-09-grilled-lamb-kebabs-tzatziki/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1/4 cup freshly squeezed lemon juice (2 lemons)`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` includes `{ \"amount\": \"2\", \"unit\": \
\"lemons\" }` in addition to the real `1/4 cup` quantity. The parenthetical is \
a yield hint, not a second measurable amount.\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-13887-pajeon-korean-scallion-pancake.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-13887-pajeon-korean-scallion-pancake/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1 cup (5 ounces/142 grams) all-purpose flour`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` becomes `1 cup`, `{ \"amount\": \"5\", \
\"unit\": null }`, and `{ \"amount\": \"125\", \"unit\": \"g\" }`. The \
source’s explicit `5 ounces/142 grams` alternate measurements are not \
preserved; the pipeline instead invents a unitless `5` and a conflicting \
derived gram value.\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-12368-pan-seared-strip-steaks.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-12368-pan-seared-strip-steaks/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `2 (12- to 16-ounce) boneless strip steaks, 1½ inches \
thick, trimmed`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` is `{ \"amount\": \"2\", \"unit\": null }` \
plus `{ \"amount\": \"12\", \"unit\": null }`, which drops the ounce unit and \
range context entirely.\n\
\n\
  - `data/pipeline-snapshots/seriouseats-com_tartiflette-recipe-5217300.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/seriouseats-com_tartiflette-recipe-5217300/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1 to 2 tablespoons (15 to 30g) unsalted butter, only \
if needed`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` is `{ \"amount\": \"1 to 2\", \"unit\": \
\"tbsp\" }` plus `{ \"amount\": \"15\", \"unit\": null }`, which drops the \
rest of the alternate metric quantity.\n\
\n\
These malformed `measurements` are a parsing bug, not just awkward source \
formatting. The parser should either preserve alternate quantities faithfully \
with units or ignore parenthetical yield hints, but it should not emit \
unitless fragments or conflicting derived values.\n\
\n\
Additional examples found 2026-04-27:\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-12228-ultracreamy-hummus.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-12228-ultracreamy-hummus/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1/3 cup lemon juice (2 lemons), plus extra for \
seasoning`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` includes `{ \"amount\": \"2\", \"unit\": \
\"lemons\" }` alongside the real `1/3 cup`. `(2 lemons)` is a yield hint, not \
an alternate quantity.\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-16428-mesquite-grilled-tacos-rasurados.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/americastestkitchen-com_recipes-16428-mesquite-grilled-tacos-rasurados/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1 (3½- to 4-pound) rack beef back ribs (about 7 \
bones)`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` is `[{ \"amount\": \"1\", \"unit\": null \
}, { \"amount\": \"3\", \"unit\": null }, { \"amount\": \"7\", \"unit\": \
\"bones\" }]`. The pound unit and range context are dropped; \"7 bones\" is a \
yield hint that became a phantom measurement.\n\
\n\
  - Same snapshot: `12 (6-inch) flour tortillas , warmed` produced \
`measurements` `[{ \"amount\": \"12\", \"unit\": null }, { \"amount\": \"6\", \
\"unit\": \"inch\" }]`. The size descriptor `(6-inch)` should not be a \
quantity.\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/seriouseats-com_ultimate-fully-loaded-nachos.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/seriouseats-com_ultimate-fully-loaded-nachos/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1/2 cup cooked black beans from one (15-ounce) can, \
drained and rinsed`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` is `[{ \"amount\": \"0.5\", \"unit\": \
\"cup\" }, { \"amount\": \"15\", \"unit\": \"oz\" }, { \"amount\": \"425\", \
\"unit\": \"g\" }]`. The 15-ounce can size is the package, not the amount of \
beans called for; treating it as a measurement implies you need 15 oz of \
beans.\n\
\n\
  - \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/cooking-nytimes-com_recipes-1021971-potato-and-leek-focaccia.json`\n\
    Cached HTML: \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/cooking-nytimes-com_recipes-1021971-potato-and-leek-focaccia/response.bin`\n\
    Source ingredient: `1 3/4 cups/420 milliliters warm water (about 100 \
degrees)`\n\
    Snapshot output: `measurements` includes `{ \"amount\": \"100\", \"unit\": \
\"degrees\" }`. The temperature parenthetical is a hint about how warm the \
water should be, not a quantity to measure.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
